course: dictionary
lesson: 2544
title: Defiant: standing firm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Defiant means refusing to give in. A defiant person will not obey, or stands firm against someone stronger. «A defiant child folded his arms» shows a child who will not do what he is asked. Folded arms and a set face are the clues.
explain: The same word can also mean brave. «A defiant shout against the storm» shows someone standing up to something much bigger than themselves. Ask: who or what is being stood up to? If it is a teacher, it may be naughty. If it is a storm, it may be brave.
explain: Look at the words around defiant. Phrases like defiant look, defiant mood and defiant to the end show how it is used. «Strong-willed» means defiant, so if you know strong-willed, you already have a close meaning.
fact: Defiant means openly refusing to obey or to do what you are told.
fact: Defiant can also mean bravely standing up to something stronger.
fact: «Strong-willed» means defiant, refusing to obey.
fact: «Strong personality» on a report often means bossy or defiant.
fact: «Threenager» is a jokey word for a defiant three-year-old acting like a moody teenager.
exercise: «A defiant child folded his arms.» What does defiant mean here? | Happy to help the teacher | Feeling very cold | Running very fast | *Refusing to obey
exercise: «A defiant shout against the storm.» What is defiant doing in this sentence? | *Bravely standing up to something stronger | Hiding from the rain | Falling asleep | Quietly asking for help
exercise: A report says «strong personality». What does it often mean? | Always early | *Bossy or defiant | Good at sport | Very shy and quiet
test: «The defiant girl stayed in her seat when the bell rang.» What does defiant show? | Wanting to go outside | Being very kind to others | *Refusing to do what she is told | Feeling sleepy after lunch
test: Which word means the same as defiant in «strong-willed»? | Hungry | *Refusing to obey | Gentle | Lost
exam: Which use of defiant shows bravery, not naughtiness? | A defiant child folded his arms | A defiant mood at breakfast | A defiant look at the teacher | *A defiant shout against the storm
